

====================================================================
AVONE LAUNCH COMMANDS 
====================================================================


====================================================================
MAIN CONTROL BRINGUP
====================================================================

Command:
  ros2 launch avone avone_control_bringup.launch.py

What this launches with individual commands:
    - Generates robot_description from xacro (URDF)
    - Publishes TF and joint states via robot_state_publisher
    - Starts ros2_control and loads the Ackermann steering controller
    - Spawns joint_state_broadcaster, then steering controller (sequenced)
    - Relays controller odometry TF into /tf
    - Starts cmd_vel filtering
    - Launches teleop control for manual testing
    - Optionally launches RViz after controllers are active






=====================
GPS BRINGUP
=====================

Command:
 ros2 launch avone avone_gps_bringup.launch.py

What this launches:
    - Starts the NMEA GPS serial driver
    - Publishes GPS fixes from a USB serial device
    - Sets the GPS frame for localisation integration
    - Converts GPS heading output into an IMU-compatible message
    - Provides heading data for robot_localization and navigation

Individual Commdands:

• GPS serial driver (NMEA)
  - Reads GPS data from USB serial
  - Publishes NavSatFix messages
  - Sets GPS frame for localisation

  Command:
    ros2 run nmea_navsat_driver nmea_serial_driver \
      --ros-args \
      -p port:=/dev/ttyUSB1 \
      -p baud:=115200 \
      -p frame_id:=gps_link1


• GPS heading → IMU conversion
  - Converts GPS heading output into IMU-compatible data
  - Used as yaw input for robot_localization

  Command:
    ros2 run avone_localisation heading_to_imu

=====================
IMU BRINGUP
=====================

Command:
  ros2 launch avone avone_imu_bringup.launch.py

What this launches:
  - Starts the VectorNav IMU interface node
  - Initializes IMU communication and data publishing
  - Publishes IMU orientation, angular velocity, and acceleration data
  - Provides IMU data for localisation and state estimation
  - (Optional) Static transform support for IMU frame alignment

Individual Commands:

• VectorNav IMU bringup
  - Starts IMU communication
  - Publishes sensor_msgs/Imu data
  - Used as the primary IMU source for localisation

  Command:
    ros2 run avone_localisation imu_start \
      --ros-args \
      -p use_sim_time:=false

=====================
LIDAR BRINGUP
=====================

Command:
  ros2 launch avone avone_lidar_bringup.launch.py

What this launches:
  - Starts the Quanergy LiDAR client
  - Connects to the LiDAR over Ethernet
  - Publishes LiDAR scan and point cloud data
  - Publishes a static transform for the LiDAR frame
  - Starts collision detection using LiDAR data

Individual Commands:

• Quanergy LiDAR client
  - Connects to the Quanergy LiDAR over Ethernet
  - Receives raw LiDAR data
  - Publishes point cloud and scan topics

  Command:
    ros2 launch quanergy_client_ros client.launch.py \
      host:=192.168.1.57


• Static transform: laser_frame → quanergy
  - Defines fixed transform between vehicle frame and LiDAR frame
  - Used for correct TF alignment of LiDAR data

  Command:
    ros2 run tf2_ros static_transform_publisher \
      0 0 0 \
      0 0 0 \
      laser_frame quanergy


• Collision detection
  - Monitors LiDAR data for front on obsticals
  - Publishes collision CAN messaged, causing fault state
  - Used as a safety layer during autonomous operation

  Command:
    ros2 run avone_nav collision_detection

=====================
LOCALISATION BRINGUP
=====================

Command:
  ros2 launch avone avone_localisation_bringup.launch.py

What this launches:
  - Starts the local (odom-frame) EKF for vehicle state estimation
  - Starts the global (map-frame) EKF for fused global localisation
  - Launches navsat_transform to fuse GPS data into the localisation stack
  - Provides odometry and pose outputs for navigation and control
  - Establishes the full robot_localization pipeline (local + global)

Individual Commands:

• Local EKF (odom frame)
  - Fuses IMU, wheel odometry, and local sensors
  - Publishes locally consistent odometry
  - Used for control and short-horizon navigation

  Command:
    ros2 launch avone_localisation local_ekf.launch.py


• Global EKF (map frame)
  - Fuses local odometry with global corrections
  - Provides globally referenced pose estimates
  - Used for navigation, mapping, and logging

  Command:
    ros2 launch avone_localisation global_ekf.launch.py


• NavSat transform
  - Converts GPS (NavSatFix) into a local Cartesian frame
  - Aligns GPS data with IMU heading and odometry
  - Feeds transformed GPS data into the global EKF

  Command:
    ros2 launch avone_localisation navsat_transform.launch.py


--------------------------------------------------------------------

Optional: Single-EKF Localisation (All Sensors Fused)

• AV.ONE single EKF
  - Fuses IMU, wheel odometry, and GPS in a single filter
  - Publishes a unified filtered odometry output
  - Used for early bringup, testing, or simplified deployments
  - Not intended for final competition configuration

  Command:
    ros2 launch avone_localisation avone_ekf.launch.py